  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 234 PM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nDry and Warming Up Into Next Weekend:\n\nThrough the middle of the upcoming week, the longwave trough that \nprovided a chilly weekend will finally get kicked off to the \nnortheast as a shortwave slides from the Southern Plains into the \neastern Gulf. This wave will not have much moisture or punch to it \nas it slides through our area, so rain chances will be very low \n(<10%) and only across south-central GA. The cool airmass from the \nweekend will finally be shoved out, allowing highs to climb back \ninto the 60s on Tuesday and Wednesday, with overnight lows returning \nto above freezing. Behind this system, a ridge will build from the \nGulf up across the Southeast US during the second half of the week \nand into next weekend. Our stretch of dry weather will continue in \nthis setup, and temperatures will warm up to around 10F above \nnormal. Highs will climb back into the 70s for Friday and next \nweekend, with overnight lows in the 40s to near 50.",
